# PromptLab project rules

- PromptLab is a FastAPI + Pydantic v2 backend with in-memory storage. Source lives in backend/app/, tests in backend/tests/, docs in docs/, feature specs in specs/.

## Project Structure
- backend/app/models.py: Pydantic models plus generate_id() and get_current_time().
- backend/app/api.py: routes, HTTPException handling, and collection-reference checks.
- backend/app/storage.py: the Storage class and the single shared `storage` instance.
- backend/app/utils.py: pure helper functions that take and return Prompt lists or strings.
- backend/app/__init__.py: holds `__version__`. This is the only source of the app version.

## Patterns and Conventions
- Every route declares `response_model`. Create routes declare `status_code=201` and delete routes declare `status_code=204`.
- Create ids with `generate_id()` and timestamps with `get_current_time()`. Timestamps are naive UTC datetimes.
- Group code under banner comments in the form `# ============== Section Name ==============`.
- PUT replaces every editable field. Omitted `description` and `collection_id` become null.
- PATCH applies only supplied fields, using `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`.
- PUT and PATCH preserve `id` and `created_at` and refresh `updated_at`.
- A collection cannot be deleted while any prompt references it.
- Storage methods never raise for missing records. They return `None` or `False`, and api.py turns that into an HTTPException.

## Coding Standards
- Add type hints to parameters and return types in all new code. Existing route functions rely on `response_model` and `status_code` instead of return annotations, so leave those as they are.
- Do not add dependencies beyond backend/requirements.txt without asking.
- Comments explain why, not what.

## File Naming
- Python modules and test files use snake_case. Test files are `test_*.py`, and `conftest.py` is the only exception.
- Reference documents in docs/ use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.md (API_REFERENCE.md, SYSTEM_MODEL.md).
- Notes, logs, and specs use kebab-case.md (agent-effect-note.md, prompt-log.md, specs/tagging-system.md).
- Classes use PascalCase. Functions and variables use snake_case.

## Error Handling
- Raise HTTPException with a `detail` string. The response body is always `{"detail": "..."}`.
- Use these exact status codes and messages:
  - 404 "Prompt not found": a prompt id in the URL does not exist.
  - 404 "Collection not found": a collection id in the URL does not exist.
  - 400 "Collection not found": a `collection_id` in a request body references a missing collection.
  - 400 "Cannot delete collection with associated prompts": the collection still has prompts.
- Never raise 422 by hand. FastAPI returns 422 automatically when Pydantic validation fails.
- Do not catch exceptions silently. Do not change existing messages or status codes unless a spec says to.

## Testing Requirements
- Run tests from the backend directory with `python -m pytest tests/ -v`.
- Use the fixtures in backend/tests/conftest.py: `client`, `sample_prompt_data`, `sample_collection_data`, and the autouse `clear_storage`.
- Every new endpoint needs one test for success and one test for each error branch above.
- Assert both the status code and the `detail` text for error responses.
- Test through the API with TestClient. Do not call storage directly except in storage tests.

## Documentation
- Use Google-style docstrings with Args, Returns, and Raises. Docstring examples must show the real values the code returns.
- When behavior changes, update the docstring, docs/API_REFERENCE.md, and the README in the same change.

## API Reference Conventions (docs/API_REFERENCE.md)
- The health version is `__version__` from backend/app/__init__.py. Never write any other version. The status string is lowercase "healthy".
- Label every status code with its reason phrase, for example `200 OK`, `201 Created`, `204 No Content`, `400 Bad Request`, `404 Not Found`, `422 Unprocessable Entity`.
- Every JSON example must be valid JSON. Never use `...` or `[...]` as a placeholder. Use a real example or an empty array with `"total": 0`.
- Every endpoint that accepts a request body documents the 422 response.
- Curl commands use `-i`, a quoted URL, and the placeholders `PROMPT_ID` and `COLLECTION_ID`. Get real ids from the POST response.
- Document PUT and PATCH semantics exactly as described under Patterns and Conventions.
- Authentication: none is implemented. Say so.
